      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you explain what is happening, see may suggestion below.\n\n```suggestion\nBazel: Drop mocha type lib from plugin API compile\n\nThe plugin_api_compiled target extends //plugins:tsconfig-plugins-base,\nwhich sets types \u003d [\"mocha\"] so plugin tests see Mocha globals. The API\npackage has no tests and no node_modules dep, so tsc cannot resolve the\ntype lib and the release build fails:\n\n  error TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for \u0027mocha\u0027.\n\nOverride types to [] in the inline tsconfig. This drops the test-only\nlib at the source and matches tsconfig.publish.json, instead of pulling\nthe whole dev node_modules tree into a pure-types compile.\n\n```",
